	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44057</id><title>African Farmers Demand Affordable Finance as Governments Fall Short on Funding</title><updated>2026-09-16T08:33:19-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44057" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Rwandan-President-Paul-Kagame-speaking-to-the-youths-during-the-Africa-Food-Systems-Forum-at-Kigali-Convention-Centre.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpeg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Rwandan-President-Paul-Kagame-speaking-to-the-youths-during-the-Africa-Food-Systems-Forum-at-Kigali-Convention-Centre.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Rwandan-President-Paul-Kagame-speaking-to-the-youths-during-the-Africa-Food-Systems-Forum-at-Kigali-Convention-Centre.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe-100x100.jpeg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Rwandan-President-Paul-Kagame-speaking-to-the-youths-during-the-Africa-Food-Systems-Forum-at-Kigali-Convention-Centre.-Credit-Farai-Shawn-Matiashe.jpeg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
KIGALI, September 16 (IPS)  - Agriculture remains underfunded in Africa as governments struggle to deliver on decades-old promises to dedicate 10% of national income to agriculture.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44057&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “African Farmers Demand Affordable Finance as Governments Fall Short on Funding”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44059</id><title>Killing of Environmental Defenders Reflects Power Struggle Over World’s Resources</title><updated>2026-09-16T08:13:55-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44059" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/DEFENDERS-1.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/DEFENDERS-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/DEFENDERS-1-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/DEFENDERS-1.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
LONDON &amp; SRINAGAR, India, September 16 (IPS)  - At least 124 land and environmental defenders were killed around the world in 2025 while protecting forests, rivers, farmland and Indigenous territories, according to a &lt;a href=&quot;https://globalwitness.org/en/press-releases/at-least-124-land-and-environmental-defenders-killed-globally-in-2025/&quot;&gt;new report by Global Witness&lt;/a&gt; that warns violence against activists remains widespread even as recorded killings have declined from previous years.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44059&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Killing of Environmental Defenders Reflects Power Struggle Over World’s Resources”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44055</id><title>One Man’s Quest to End Female Genital Mutilation (FGM) in Mali</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:49:46-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44055" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Sidi-Haidara_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Sidi-Haidara_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Sidi-Haidara_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Sidi-Haidara_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, September 16 (IPS)  - In Mali, an estimated nine out of ten women and girls have undergone &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unwomen.org/en/articles/faqs/faqs-on-female-genital-mutilation-causes-impact-and-how-to-end-it&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;female genital mutilation (FGM)&lt;/a&gt;. And for years, Sidi Haidara, a father and recognized leader in his community, believed the practice was simply part of life.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44055&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “One Man’s Quest to End Female Genital Mutilation (FGM) in Mali”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44056</id><title>Renewed Hostilities In Yemen Inflame Displacement and Regional Risks</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:25:28-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44056" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Khaled-Khiari.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Khaled-Khiari.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Khaled-Khiari-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Khaled-Khiari.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, September 16 (IPS)  - In recent days, the humanitarian situation in Yemen has deteriorated sharply following a new escalation of hostilities between the Iran-backed Houthi rebels and the Saudi-backed Presidential Leadership Council (PLC). This follows four years of relative stability, marking the most severe resurgence of violence since the collapse of the United Nations (UN)-mediated ceasefire in October 2022.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44056&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Renewed Hostilities In Yemen Inflame Displacement and Regional Risks”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44065</id><title>World News in Brief: Shipping alert from IMO, democracy vanishing in Nicaragua, alert over political ‘denialism’</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44065" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/08-09-2026_Adobe_ship.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/08-09-2026_Adobe_ship.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/08-09-2026_Adobe_ship.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/08-09-2026_Adobe_ship.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Amid a rising number of attacks on shipping in key waterways in the Middle East linked to the US-Iran war, the head of UN maritime agency, Mr. Arsenio Dominguez, has insisted that the conflict is not a “pretext” to target “innocent seafarers”.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44065&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “World News in Brief: Shipping alert from IMO, democracy vanishing in Nicaragua, alert over political ‘denialism’”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44064</id><title>Repression continues in Venezuela in the face of ‘appalling’ human rights violations</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44064" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_Adobe_Caracas.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_Adobe_Caracas.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_Adobe_Caracas.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_Adobe_Caracas.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In Venezuela’s El Rodeo maximum security prison, some of those detained for political reasons are subject to forced intubation – and prolonged confinement in a sealed underground cistern. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44064&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Repression continues in Venezuela in the face of ‘appalling’ human rights violations”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44063</id><title>AI, climate and conflicts top Guterres’s agenda ahead of General Assembly</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44063" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_UNP_Guterres_presser.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_UNP_Guterres_presser.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_UNP_Guterres_presser.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026_UNP_Guterres_presser.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ahead of the UN General Assembly’s high-level week, Secretary-General António Guterres said the world had entered “an era of deep uncertainty” and urged governments to embrace international cooperation to address global threats.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44063&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “AI, climate and conflicts top Guterres’s agenda ahead of General Assembly”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44062</id><title>Security Council LIVE: ‘Being a woman is a crime in Afghanistan,’ civil society briefer declares</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44062" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/15-05-2026-IOM-Afghanistan-04.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/15-05-2026-IOM-Afghanistan-04.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/15-05-2026-IOM-Afghanistan-04.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/15-05-2026-IOM-Afghanistan-04.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since the Taliban returned to power in Afghanistan in 2021, the continuing presence of terrorist groups as well as rights violations against women and girls are a growing concern as the Security Council met Wednesday to hear latest developments, including from a civil society representative who said being born as a woman in the country “is a crime”. Follow full coverage here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44062&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Security Council LIVE: ‘Being a woman is a crime in Afghanistan,’ civil society briefer declares”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44061</id><title>Gaza: At least 20 killed in deadly building collapse, search for survivors continues</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44061" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026-Gaza-UNRWA-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026-Gaza-UNRWA-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026-Gaza-UNRWA-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/09/16-09-2026-Gaza-UNRWA-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Search and rescue operations continued in Gaza City on Wednesday following the collapse of a bombed-out building that killed at least 20 people, according to reports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44061&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Gaza: At least 20 killed in deadly building collapse, search for survivors continues”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44060</id><title>UN report warns of reprisals against those who collaborate in defence of human rights</title><updated>2026-09-16T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44060" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/assets/2017/02/26788/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/assets/2017/02/26788/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/assets/2017/02/26788/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/assets/2017/02/26788/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Activists, lawyers and others who cooperate with the United Nations on human rights continue to face intimidation and reprisals, according to a new report issued on Wednesday by the Secretary-General that calls for greater protection and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/09/16/44060&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN report warns of reprisals against those who collaborate in defence of human rights”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0005s ch:1 -->